WEBVTT

00:04.460 --> 00:06.750
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

00:07.170 --> 00:11.580
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

00:13.380 --> 00:17.040
The rain's still going strong. And it's a holiday, too.

00:20.330 --> 00:23.920
It's like the gloom of a rainy day
even makes us feel gloomy, too.

00:24.040 --> 00:27.290
You think so? I like the rain.

00:27.750 --> 00:30.380
That's 'cause I can shamelessly stay at home!

00:30.880 --> 00:33.880
People suck it up and go to work
even on rainy days, you know.

00:34.920 --> 00:39.170
The goddess summoned
from another world enshrined here...

00:39.580 --> 00:42.080
was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

02:13.130 --> 02:17.670
<b>EPISODE 9</b>

02:16.880 --> 02:20.830
Okay, done shopping!
I've finished all my tasks for the day!

02:21.420 --> 02:25.330
A-after this, I'm gonna spend all day
reading manga under the kotatsu!

02:25.540 --> 02:27.580
After all, it's raining outside!

02:27.960 --> 02:32.500
I have no choice but to hole up here!
Since it's raining outside!

02:32.710 --> 02:35.460
The rain really pumps you up, huh?

02:36.040 --> 02:37.130
Th-that's true!

02:37.330 --> 02:42.040
The newest volume came out recently, so I think
I'll reread the whole graphic series from volume 1!

02:42.330 --> 02:43.880
Koito, make some tea!

02:44.130 --> 02:45.130
Sure.

02:45.790 --> 02:49.250
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

02:49.250 --> 02:52.710
<b>Plastic Mask</b>

02:49.250 --> 02:52.710
<b>Plastic Mask</b>

02:49.250 --> 02:52.710
<b>Plastic Mask</b>

02:52.710 --> 02:55.540
<b>Plastic Mask</b>

02:53.460 --> 02:55.290
This is interesting.

02:55.540 --> 03:00.000
<b>Plastic Mask</b>

02:55.830 --> 02:59.830
Isn't it? It's a very long novel that's been going on
for more than 40 years.

03:00.330 --> 03:02.170
Wow, impressive.

03:02.420 --> 03:10.500
But, going on for that long can be detrimental.
Like it's supposed to be set in the 1970s...

03:10.710 --> 03:11.290
Yeah.

03:11.920 --> 03:14.290
But in the newest volume, there's a smartphone.

03:14.750 --> 03:15.750
Oh, really?

03:17.210 --> 03:21.380
Ah, I'm done with this one.
Elda, are you still reading volume 7?

03:21.580 --> 03:24.460
I-I'm reading it right now, so give me a minute.

03:27.830 --> 03:29.750
Elda! There's a leak!

03:30.000 --> 03:30.630
Huh?

03:32.250 --> 03:36.540
M-my manga and game collection and toy shelf!

03:36.710 --> 03:40.710
Wh-wh-wh-what do I do?! C-c-call the police!

03:41.460 --> 03:43.670
Calm down! Just calm down for now!

03:43.750 --> 03:46.500
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

03:46.710 --> 03:48.330
I managed to save them...

03:48.790 --> 03:52.830
My manga and game collection and my toys...

03:53.250 --> 03:57.460
When I asked Grandpa, he said that there's
copper roofing above the inner shrine.

03:58.000 --> 04:00.000
It seems to crack sometimes.

04:00.750 --> 04:03.080
This is something we have to call a carpenter for.

04:03.460 --> 04:07.420
Huh?! A carpenter is coming?! Into my room?!

04:07.710 --> 04:10.380
Well, we can't just leave it like this.

04:10.380 --> 04:13.330
N-no, it's fine how it is now, right?

04:13.790 --> 04:18.040
I-I mean, they say the sound of water
has relaxation effects...

04:18.330 --> 04:20.540
Keeping it like this is kinda elegant.

04:20.670 --> 04:24.790
What're you talking about? If it doesn't get fixed properly,
your manga and everything will get moldy!

04:24.790 --> 04:27.380
Huh?! Th-that is a problem!

04:27.580 --> 04:30.630
Yeah. That's why we have
to get a carpenter to come here.

04:30.960 --> 04:33.960
B-but... if he sees a room like this...

04:35.630 --> 04:36.880
If he sees a room like this...?

04:37.080 --> 04:39.170
Word will get out that I'm an otaku!

04:39.960 --> 04:41.880
The entire city already knows.

04:46.460 --> 04:51.130
Grandpa made the call for us.
He said the carpenter is heading over now.

04:51.330 --> 04:56.000
H-how could my beloved rainy day have a trap like this?

04:56.540 --> 04:59.000
Well, we do live in an old building.

04:59.670 --> 05:00.330
I know!

05:01.460 --> 05:03.580
The carpenter is coming here anyways,

05:03.710 --> 05:06.920
so let's take this chance to remodel this place
into a designer inner shrine.

05:07.580 --> 05:09.670
"Designer inner shrine"?

05:07.880 --> 05:09.540
<b>Designer inner shrine</b>

05:10.170 --> 05:13.540
Yes! Make it two stories, and give it a stairwell!

05:13.960 --> 05:16.130
And the walls will be like undressed concrete!

05:16.380 --> 05:18.460
Huh. It looks unsettling.

05:18.830 --> 05:22.290
Ah, b-but, I might want a game room or something!

05:22.750 --> 05:27.210
With acoustics and a monsterous 100-inch big screen!

05:27.540 --> 05:32.750
I want to make a balcony!
One that feels like you'd have a fancy breakfast there!

05:33.290 --> 05:38.040
And one wall will have a glass case
for displaying plastic models and figures!

05:38.500 --> 05:40.500
Let's go ask Grandpa about it right now!

05:41.500 --> 05:44.500
O-okay! Kikujiro is in the shrine office!

05:50.920 --> 05:52.330
He was raging mad.

05:52.710 --> 05:54.210
He sure was.

05:57.790 --> 06:00.330
It keeps raining harder.

06:00.880 --> 06:04.790
Didn't Koyuzu go shopping? I hope she's all right.

06:05.290 --> 06:10.540
I made her take a raincoat just in case,
so she should be okay.

06:10.830 --> 06:16.460
A raincoat, huh? The latest ones
are so effectively waterproof it's amazing.

06:17.330 --> 06:20.460
Speaking of, what did you do
in the Edo Period when it rained?

06:20.960 --> 06:23.670
Did you wear a hat like this?

06:23.920 --> 06:25.630
You mean a rain hat?

06:25.750 --> 06:29.330
Hmm... By the middle of the Edo period,
rain umbrellas had already been replaced

06:29.330 --> 06:32.080
by umbrellas like the ones we have now.

06:32.380 --> 06:34.000
Huh, really?

06:34.580 --> 06:37.710
Women's hairstyles had become intricate things.

06:38.080 --> 06:41.710
Since putting a hat on the head would ruin the style,

06:41.880 --> 06:45.880
the hand-held "umbrella" grew popular
among the common folk.

06:47.000 --> 06:48.920
There were so many different types.

06:49.130 --> 06:51.380
Like the cheap and sturdy "bangasa,"

06:50.540 --> 06:52.460
<b>Bangasa</b>

06:50.540 --> 06:52.460
<b>(sturdy oilpaper umbrella)</b>

06:51.670 --> 06:53.960
and the long-handled "Tsumaorigasa"
that court nobles, and Buddhist priests,

06:53.960 --> 06:56.040
and the like carried in certain ceremonies.

06:54.580 --> 06:56.130
<b>Tsumaorigasa</b>

06:54.580 --> 06:56.130
<b>(folding umbrella)</b>

06:56.960 --> 06:58.670
Haira-sama had one of those, too, right?

06:58.880 --> 07:04.540
Haira's is a "Janomegasa."
When you spread it out, the edges have a ring pattern.

07:04.920 --> 07:08.880
It's an umbrella that women and celebrities carry.
It's fairly expensive.

07:09.080 --> 07:12.540
Huh? That was a really fancy one.

07:12.960 --> 07:16.790
I really wish I could have a mature,
high-fashion brand umbrella, too.

07:17.250 --> 07:20.830
Rental umbrellas were popular for people like that.

07:21.210 --> 07:22.330
They borrowed umbrellas?

07:22.580 --> 07:27.540
At large stores like Echigoya, when it suddenly rained,
they'd have rentable umbrellas for customers.

07:27.540 --> 07:29.420
<b>Kashigasa</b>

07:27.540 --> 07:29.420
<b>(rental umbrella)</b>

07:27.750 --> 07:31.920
The shop name was written on the umbrella, and the
customer was made into a walking advertisement.

07:32.210 --> 07:34.790
Edo natives also hold vanity in high regard.

07:35.130 --> 07:38.790
Holding umbrellas from a major store
also showed status.

07:39.250 --> 07:44.290
I totally get it! I use the brand paper bag that I got
when I bought my purse with a whole lot of care!

07:46.330 --> 07:52.000
Yeah... that already tattered paper bag. Let it go, already!

07:52.000 --> 07:54.080
No way, I can still use it!

08:07.170 --> 08:10.000
Looks like the sheet copper on the roof was cracked.

08:10.000 --> 08:12.210
It'll get a temporary fix for now.

08:12.500 --> 08:13.880
O-oh, I see.

08:14.330 --> 08:16.790
I feel bad that it has to be done in the rain.

08:18.670 --> 08:21.210
I-I'm home...

08:21.500 --> 08:23.630
Whoa, Koyuzu! You're completely drenched!

08:23.630 --> 08:25.330
A-are you all right?!

08:26.170 --> 08:29.580
Everything not under the raincoat is soaked.

08:31.880 --> 08:36.670
I wonder if the raincoat is too small now.
Guess I'll buy a new one.

08:36.790 --> 08:39.210
Huh? Don't bother, it'd be a waste.

08:39.540 --> 08:43.880
The granny at Fujimart told me
that my kappa was very cute!

08:44.460 --> 08:45.170
Oh yeah?

08:45.540 --> 08:49.420
By the way, why do we call raincoats "kappa"?

08:49.670 --> 08:51.290
Huh? I wonder why.

08:52.540 --> 08:56.210
Kappa... maybe because it's that thing
with a plate on it's head?

08:53.130 --> 08:55.170
<b>Kappa</b>

08:56.630 --> 08:58.830
Like even if it gets soaked by rain, it doesn't mind!

08:58.960 --> 09:02.080
Oh! That must be why! You're so smart, Big Sis!

09:02.080 --> 09:04.500
H-hold it right there, you chummy sisters!

09:05.500 --> 09:07.710
There are various theories
about the origin of the word "kappa."

09:08.250 --> 09:11.540
Like that it's from "capa,"
the word for "cover" in Portuguese,

09:11.790 --> 09:14.710
or that when we shorten "kamipaori" we get "kappa."

09:14.880 --> 09:15.880
Wow.

09:14.960 --> 09:16.130
<b>Kamipaori</b>

09:14.960 --> 09:16.130
<b>(paper half-coat)</b>

09:16.460 --> 09:21.290
The theory I like is it gets its name from the similarity
of it's shape to when birds have both wings together,

09:21.290 --> 09:24.420
so it's written as "kappa" meaning a bird
with it's wings together.

09:22.750 --> 09:24.130
<b>Kappa</b>

09:22.750 --> 09:24.130
<b>(wings together)</b>

09:25.420 --> 09:28.040
That's very pretty!

09:28.040 --> 09:32.790
Isn't it? W-well, I was more of a fan
of the mino than the kappa.

09:33.000 --> 09:36.250
Are "mino" the straw raincoats the ones
that those namahage demons wear?

09:36.580 --> 09:40.920
Yes, exactly. Until kappa became popular,
straw raincoats were mainstream.

09:41.250 --> 09:46.710
By the way, I was invincible, wrapped up
in a straw raincoat with a rain hat on my head!

09:41.290 --> 09:50.330
<b>INVINCIBLE</b>

09:47.250 --> 09:50.130
You look like a big, tall bagworm...

09:50.460 --> 09:55.040
But thinking back on it, the umbrella is the only one
that hasn't changed at all.

09:55.040 --> 09:57.250
It's kept the same shape for hundreds of years.

09:57.630 --> 10:00.420
Nowadays there are umbrellas
that open upside down, you know.

10:00.830 --> 10:04.790
But it's still umbrella-shaped, right? Kinda like...

10:04.790 --> 10:06.960
It's super convenient! And stuff.

10:06.960 --> 10:08.880
Uh, umm...

10:09.210 --> 10:11.250
Oh, I was thinking about this earlier,

10:11.380 --> 10:14.880
but it's inconvenient that there's a hand you can't use
because you're holding the umbrella.

10:14.920 --> 10:15.710
That's true!

10:16.250 --> 10:19.460
How about hanging an umbrella
that opens upside-down on a drone?

10:16.920 --> 10:22.420
<b>INVINCIBLE</b>

10:19.750 --> 10:22.290
Now you can go out with your hands free!

10:22.460 --> 10:24.000
Oh, that might work!

10:24.250 --> 10:27.040
B-but, won't Drone-san get wet?

10:27.540 --> 10:32.040
The drone will be waterproof!
Getting wet won't break it, so it's fine!

10:32.420 --> 10:36.880
B-but, but... I feel bad that Drone-san
is the only one who gets wet!

10:37.000 --> 10:40.000
Poor thing! Poor thing! Poor thing! Poor thing! Poor thing!

10:39.080 --> 10:40.000
Ba-bump!

10:42.130 --> 10:45.210
Goodness! Such a good kid!

10:46.000 --> 10:49.460
Th-then, I'll hold an umbrella open for the drone.

10:50.670 --> 10:56.830
<b>INVINCIBLE</b>

10:50.670 --> 10:56.830
<b>INVINCIBLE</b>

10:51.380 --> 10:53.420
Now the drone won't get wet either.

10:53.420 --> 10:54.580
Hooray!

10:54.580 --> 10:56.330
So in the end, it's a flop?

11:08.630 --> 11:10.500
Oh! The rain stopped!

11:10.630 --> 11:13.710
It has! The skies are clear now, this is great!

11:14.080 --> 11:18.130
I love rainy days, but it's a problem
when it just keeps raining, huh?

11:20.580 --> 11:23.750
Sis, it's the after-rain smell!

11:24.040 --> 11:26.920
Yup! I love this smell!

11:39.170 --> 11:42.710
O-okay! The rain has stopped, so...

11:42.830 --> 11:44.750
Yeah! Let's go outside!

11:44.750 --> 11:46.580
I'm staying inside!

11:47.420 --> 11:48.080
Huh?

11:48.080 --> 11:48.750
Huh?

11:49.170 --> 11:49.830
Eh?

12:01.380 --> 12:04.830
Hmm... It's gotten pretty messy.

12:04.830 --> 12:06.790
Guess I'll do a bit of cleaning.

12:07.460 --> 12:12.420
I'll sell the things I don't want to the tanuki store...
and pull some weeds...

12:12.540 --> 12:14.290
Whoa, my turnips are spoiled!

12:17.330 --> 12:20.170
All right, it's sparkling clean now!

12:22.420 --> 12:28.210
Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto, why is the miko
pulling on your cheeks? Any idea why?

12:28.670 --> 12:31.790
B-because my room is a mess!

12:31.920 --> 12:37.540
Your stuff's been out of your closet ever since the leak!
Do you think your cleaning should be done in-game?!

12:38.210 --> 12:43.170
N-no, somehow once I take things out
I can't fit them all back in...

12:43.380 --> 12:46.580
Why can't I fit all the things that were in it before?

12:48.330 --> 12:53.460
Then this is a good opportunity
to rearrange your closet. I'll help you with it.

12:53.580 --> 12:55.790
O-okay, thanks.

12:56.170 --> 12:59.580
Now, first of all, let's start cleaning
with the small stuff lying around.

12:59.960 --> 13:04.040
Ouch! I-I stepped on something hard!

13:05.920 --> 13:07.670
A-a toy block?!

13:07.790 --> 13:12.080
B-be careful! Those are the LOGO blocks
that I tried to make a super cool robot out of,

13:12.210 --> 13:14.500
but I gave up really quickly!

13:14.790 --> 13:18.330
I also stepped on them a lot yesterday, and it hurt!

13:18.580 --> 13:20.330
Put it away as soon as that happens!

13:20.670 --> 13:25.960
There's still a ton of LOGO blocks everywhere...
This is akin to a field of landmines, Koito!

13:25.960 --> 13:28.790
This is main hall of a supposedly peaceful shrine!

13:31.630 --> 13:35.000
Phew, now we can clean up with ease.

13:35.670 --> 13:38.250
Let's take out everything in the closet for now.

13:38.460 --> 13:42.960
We should divide the things you'll use soon
with the things you won't use soon and rearrange them.

13:43.380 --> 13:48.540
I-I see... So things I hardly use,
I should put in the warehouse or somewhere?

13:48.750 --> 13:54.330
That's right. Since the things in the closet
unexpectedly go unused, you won't lose any of it.

13:54.420 --> 14:03.380
<b>Will Not</b>

13:54.420 --> 14:03.380
<b>Use Soon</b>

13:54.420 --> 14:03.380
<b>Will Use</b>

13:54.420 --> 14:03.380
<b>Soon</b>

13:55.630 --> 13:58.170
Now, sort everything into this "Will Use Soon Box"

13:58.170 --> 14:00.790
and this "Will Not Use Soon Box."

14:01.000 --> 14:03.330
O-okay, here I go!

14:03.580 --> 14:07.420
Um, what did I put in this box again?

14:10.080 --> 14:13.790
Oh! This brings back memories!
Maybe I'll play with this since it's been so long!

14:13.790 --> 14:16.420
<b>Will Use Soon</b>

14:14.210 --> 14:15.830
Into the "Will Use Soon Box."

14:16.750 --> 14:18.670
Um, next up...

14:21.080 --> 14:25.670
Waaah! I forgot I had this!
Maybe I'll play with this since it's been so long!

14:25.580 --> 14:27.790
<b>Will Use Soon</b>

14:25.830 --> 14:27.500
Into the "Will Use Soon Box."

14:29.630 --> 14:32.670
Ah! I customized this one quite a bit!

14:34.670 --> 14:39.330
Aaah! I collected a lot of these, too!
Maybe I'll play with them since it's been so long!

14:39.790 --> 14:41.080
"Will Use Soon Box."

14:40.830 --> 14:41.670
<b>Will Use Soon</b>

14:41.670 --> 14:46.630
<b>Will Not</b>

14:41.670 --> 14:46.630
<b>Use Soon</b>

14:41.710 --> 14:44.040
Should we put both of them in this one?

14:44.250 --> 14:46.130
Er... y-yes.

14:50.630 --> 14:54.000
Have we finally done about half of it?
This is taking forever.

14:54.630 --> 14:56.500
When was the last time you organized this?

14:56.920 --> 14:59.630
M-must be about 400 years ago, I think.

15:00.210 --> 15:01.960
That's why this is taking forever.

15:04.250 --> 15:06.920
This reminds of "susuhaki" in the Edo days.

15:07.040 --> 15:08.250
Susuhaki?

15:08.500 --> 15:10.170
It means "sweeping the soot away".

15:10.170 --> 15:13.630
In the Edo days, a deep clean was done
on December 13th.

15:13.790 --> 15:17.830
Oh, we do a New Year's "great purification"
to sweep the soot away, too!

15:17.960 --> 15:22.080
Yes, yes. Well, that was more of a ritual.

15:19.000 --> 15:21.290
<b>Sweeping the soot away</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:27.710
In Edo, since things like ink and candles
for heating and light were regularly used,

15:27.710 --> 15:30.960
the furniture and the ceilings
would become pitch black with soot.

15:31.210 --> 15:34.290
That's why we'd brush it all away
with long bamboo poles.

15:34.750 --> 15:38.080
Wow, but why December 13th?

15:38.420 --> 15:41.830
On December 13th, at the reigning shogun residences,

15:41.830 --> 15:45.750
there was soot-cleaning event called
"The Grand Soot-Sweeping Occasion."

15:46.040 --> 15:50.500
In accordance with that, everyone from the feudal lords
to the commonfolk started doing it all on the same day.

15:50.880 --> 15:53.920
Then you also worked hard to clean
with the bamboo poles, right?

15:54.040 --> 15:58.040
<b>Rub</b>

15:54.040 --> 15:58.040
<b>Rub</b>

15:54.040 --> 15:58.040
<b>Rub</b>

15:54.040 --> 15:58.040
<b>Rub</b>

15:54.540 --> 15:59.250
I tried to spread soot on my own face
and pretend that I was done cleaning,

15:58.040 --> 16:06.750
<b>Heh heh...</b>

15:58.040 --> 16:06.750
<b>Perfection...</b>

15:59.580 --> 16:03.130
but I did it while my room was still messy
so I got caught and was scolded by my miko.

16:03.130 --> 16:06.290
I wonder why you put your efforts
towards the wrong things...

16:09.250 --> 16:11.830
Okay! We've tidied up pretty well in here!

16:12.040 --> 16:13.790
W-we just have a little bit left!

16:14.000 --> 16:17.830
Let's see... this box is... hm?

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>Good day, Katoken</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>You Weren't in my Dreams</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>It's 7! Everyone Huddle!</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>Quiz! I get it now!</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>Friend City</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>Tacchan Kacchan</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.500
<b>Magical Pine</b>

16:18.790 --> 16:20.170
What are these?

16:20.630 --> 16:24.790
They're video tapes. You don't know about them?
You record TV programs on them.

16:24.920 --> 16:28.960
Ah! So this is the video tape thing!
This is my first time seeing one!

16:29.210 --> 16:32.790
Well, nowadays when it comes to recording,
you use a hard disk, huh?

16:33.540 --> 16:36.380
Oh, I might want to watch the Drifters stuff I recorded.

16:37.540 --> 16:38.170
Huh?

16:38.250 --> 16:42.960
<b>Good day, Katoken</b>

16:38.250 --> 16:42.960
<b>You Weren't in my Dreams</b>

16:38.250 --> 16:42.960
<b>It's 7! Everyone Huddle!</b>

16:38.250 --> 16:42.960
<b>Tacchan Kacchan</b>

16:38.250 --> 16:42.960
<b>Friend City</b>

16:38.750 --> 16:41.040
There's a single small one here.

16:41.040 --> 16:42.580
It doesn't have a title, either.

16:43.210 --> 16:50.290
Yeah, that's a video that Shimaden took. Was it 20 years
ago? They suddenly came and recorded the shrine.

16:50.290 --> 16:54.460
Eh, Takamimi Shrine from the past is on here?! In this?!

16:54.670 --> 16:56.080
And you're there, too?!

16:56.380 --> 16:57.920
Yes, I would be.

16:58.460 --> 17:01.420
But I don't think it was for a festival or a ritual or anything,

17:01.420 --> 17:05.750
they just made a recording
because they had tape left over.

17:05.960 --> 17:07.790
Wow, I wanna see it!

17:08.250 --> 17:11.960
It sounds interesting to watch video
from before I was born!

17:12.420 --> 17:14.250
But this is Betamax, so...

17:14.750 --> 17:15.580
Betamax?

17:15.580 --> 17:17.500
It's a different type of tape.

17:17.880 --> 17:22.540
Hmm... Shimaden might still have a Betamax player.

17:22.920 --> 17:26.750
Really?! Then I'm going to see the granny at Shimaden!

17:26.920 --> 17:29.040
Huh? Wh-what about cleaning my room?

17:29.630 --> 17:33.250
It's mostly clean, so you'll be okay
handling the rest yourself, Elda!

17:34.380 --> 17:36.080
Bye! Be back soon!

17:36.080 --> 17:38.960
Huh?! What?! I won't be okay, though!

17:39.460 --> 17:42.960
<b>Shimaden Electric</b>

17:40.000 --> 17:42.630
Huh, a Betamax tape?

17:43.290 --> 17:45.540
Now that you mention it,
we did record something like that...

17:46.250 --> 17:48.000
Did Elda have this?

17:48.130 --> 17:52.210
Yup! She said that Shimaden
might still have a player for it!

17:52.420 --> 17:56.080
A Betamax player, huh...? Where is that thing?

17:56.420 --> 17:57.830
Can I search for it with you?

17:57.960 --> 17:59.830
Yes, I'd like that, Koi-chan.

18:12.710 --> 18:17.040
It should play on this. Try pushing that button.

18:17.250 --> 18:19.000
Umm, this one?

18:21.580 --> 18:23.330
Huh? Nothing's showing up?

18:23.330 --> 18:26.170
It's rewinding, wait a second.

18:26.170 --> 18:27.710
Re...? What?

18:29.920 --> 18:32.380
Now, push the button next to it.

18:32.630 --> 18:33.210
'Kay.

18:34.960 --> 18:36.080
Oh! I see it!

18:38.330 --> 18:39.880
Wow...

18:40.580 --> 18:44.210
I didn't exist in this world yet at this time.

18:45.210 --> 18:46.960
Feels kind of mysterious...

18:48.040 --> 18:51.000
Testing, testing. Is it really recording?

18:51.380 --> 18:55.580
This is you?! Whoa! You're so young and beautiful!

18:55.750 --> 18:57.920
Don't tease me, now!

18:57.920 --> 18:59.790
Oh, Shimaden is here!

18:59.790 --> 19:01.130
Hey, that's Elda's voice.

19:03.040 --> 19:06.880
Hm? Is that a Betamax? I haven't seen that in a while...

19:07.330 --> 19:10.880
Elda... She really hasn't changed a bit.
I found it while I was cleaning out my closet.<b></b>

19:10.880 --> 19:13.710
I thought I'd let it do one last job.

19:14.000 --> 19:20.580
O-oh yeah, Shimaden, have you played FF7?!
The polygons are amazing! It's basically live-action!

19:20.750 --> 19:24.250
A-and on top of that,
I heard there's a route where Aerith lives!

19:24.250 --> 19:25.630
That isn't true.

19:26.170 --> 19:28.040
I-I've been bamboozled!

19:28.040 --> 19:30.500
Pure elves are so easily fooled by humanity!

19:30.500 --> 19:32.380
Her personality's the same, too.

19:32.960 --> 19:35.630
Eh? What're you doing, Shimaden-san?

19:35.630 --> 19:36.380
Huh?

19:36.880 --> 19:39.170
I've told you to stop using "-san" with me, Sayako.

19:39.170 --> 19:40.540
That voice...
Really?<b></b>

19:41.580 --> 19:44.000
Then you're Shimaden-chan!

19:44.380 --> 19:48.290
You're using "-chan" now?
I'm several times your age, you know.

19:48.290 --> 19:49.250
Mom...

19:49.250 --> 19:51.000
Then Shimaden-sama?

19:49.920 --> 19:51.580
This brings me back.

19:51.580 --> 19:54.080
Can't you just call me regular old "Shimaden"?

19:52.170 --> 19:55.210
Sayako was about your age at the time.

19:54.080 --> 19:59.330
Good grief, you're 16 now but you haven't changed at all.

20:00.250 --> 20:04.210
That's not true. I'm officially Elda's miko now!

20:04.330 --> 20:07.080
I'm gonna go hardcore from here on, Elda!

20:07.080 --> 20:09.960
Eh?! G-go easy on me, please...

20:11.170 --> 20:13.580
Looks like your scary miko-san has arrived!

20:17.630 --> 20:20.580
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

20:22.460 --> 20:24.500
I've more or less tidied up.

20:24.750 --> 20:25.710
I'm home.

20:27.920 --> 20:29.790
W-welcome back, Koito!

20:30.000 --> 20:32.040
What do you think? Nice and clean now, right?

20:32.040 --> 20:34.330
I'm the type that can get it done when I have...

20:37.000 --> 20:38.000
Koito?

20:38.710 --> 20:44.750
Um, you know... this tape... my mom was on it.

20:48.380 --> 20:49.460
Oh...

20:51.000 --> 20:53.830
Would you like the tape?

21:00.580 --> 21:04.330
Nah. You hang on to it, Elda.

21:07.500 --> 21:08.460
Okay.

21:15.170 --> 21:16.330
Then, Koito...

21:17.880 --> 21:19.750
Should I toss you up in the air now?

21:20.210 --> 21:20.920
What?

21:21.500 --> 21:25.960
In the Edo days, when we finished the deep cleaning,
we'd get tossed up in the air.

21:25.960 --> 21:27.250
Huh? Why?

21:27.250 --> 21:28.540
Er, I don't know.

21:28.540 --> 21:29.920
You don't know?!

21:29.920 --> 21:32.960
It may have been to ward off evil, but...

21:33.250 --> 21:36.080
"Huzzah! We're done with something tedious!"

21:36.500 --> 21:38.210
May be why it's done.

21:38.710 --> 21:42.750
W-well, I don't really mind if you want to do it.

21:43.460 --> 21:44.540
Okay then...

21:46.000 --> 21:46.670
Come.

21:46.920 --> 21:47.580
Huh?

21:47.710 --> 21:56.880
W-well... Height-wise, it's impossible for you
to lift me up, yeah? So I'll lift you up.

21:57.250 --> 21:57.960
C'mon.

21:58.750 --> 22:04.000
Uh... L-lifting me up... Th-that's, uh...

22:14.130 --> 22:16.830
Wh-what if you lift me bridal-style?

22:18.210 --> 22:20.960
What's wrong, Koito? C'mon, hurry...

22:20.960 --> 22:22.500
N-no, no, no!

22:22.500 --> 22:25.290
I-I'm a little embarrassed to do that...

22:25.460 --> 22:29.830
It's not that embarrassing. C'mon. C'mon, c'mon.

22:32.630 --> 22:34.250
It's embarrassing!

22:35.080 --> 22:37.290
Wh-why are you running away, Koito?!

22:37.500 --> 22:38.830
Let me lift you up!

22:38.830 --> 22:40.290
I don't wanna!

22:40.290 --> 22:41.790
Wow, you're fast.
